<header><div><div class="eyebrow">An eight-century field trip</div><h1>The Dominican<br><em>Time Lantern.</em></h1></div><div><p>One black-and-white habit. A surprising number of ways to light up the world. Move through time and follow the thread.</p><span class="folio">1206 — 2016 · Eight windows into a much larger story</span></div></header>
<figure class="panorama" style="margin:0"><img id="art" src="data:image/webp;base64,<?= $art ?>" alt="Original imagined panorama connecting a French convent, Italian cloister, painter’s easel, Caribbean shore and French church with a golden ribbon."><span class="stationmark" id="marker"></span><figcaption class="artcaption"><span id="artlabel">Prouille · a quiet beginning</span><span>An imagined landscape, not a historical map</span></figcaption></figure>
<section class="navigator" aria-label="Time controls"><div class="navhead"><p id="counter">Window 1 of 8 · move the lantern</p><div class="navbuttons"><button id="prev" aria-label="Previous milestone">←</button><button id="next" aria-label="Next milestone">→</button></div></div><label for="time">CHOOSE A HISTORICAL WINDOW</label><input id="time" type="range" min="0" max="7" value="0" step="1" aria-valuetext="1206, A community before an Order"><div class="rangelabels"><span>1206 / BEGINNINGS</span><span>2016 / STILL UNFOLDING</span></div></section>
<section class="content" aria-label="Selected milestone"><div><div class="eyebrow" id="thread">COMMUNITY</div><div class="year" id="year">1206</div><div class="place" id="place"></div><div class="object"><strong id="object"></strong><span id="objectnote"></span></div></div><div aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"><h2 id="title"></h2><p class="story" id="story"></p><div class="try"><b>AT THE TABLE, TOGETHER</b><span id="prompt"></span></div></div></section>
<div class="threads" aria-label="Highlight a historical thread"></div><p class="note" id="filterstatus">All eight windows are lit. The slider steps between milestones, not equal lengths of time.</p><div class="stations" aria-label="Jump to a milestone"></div>
<section class="compare"><div class="eyebrow" style="color:#84551d">The long view</div><h2>How much time fits between?</h2><div class="comparegrid"><label>FROM<select id="from" aria-label="First comparison milestone"></select></label><output id="gap" aria-live="polite"></output><label>TO<select id="to" aria-label="Second comparison milestone"></select></label></div><div class="scale" aria-hidden="true"><span id="interval"></span></div><div class="scaleEnds"><span>1206</span><span>Proportional time scale</span><span>2016</span></div><p id="comparison" aria-live="polite"></p></section>
<div class="actions"><button class="primary" id="print">Print a little journey</button><button id="restart">Start again</button><span id="visited">1 / 8 windows explored</span></div>
<footer><p>Inspired by Jon’s <a href="?source=1">Timeline of Dominican History</a>, a one-page illustrated overview he shared in 2011. This is a new, selective companion, not a reproduction of his PDF. The illustrated objects are storytelling props; the landscape is imagined.</p><p>“Dominican” here means the Order of Preachers and its wider family, not the Dominican Republic. Dates marked “c.” are approximate. No accounts, scores, or saved personal data.</p></footer><section id="paper"></section>
<noscript><p>This time lantern needs JavaScript for its controls. The Dominican Order was confirmed in 1216; its story includes Thomas Aquinas, Catherine of Siena, Fra Angelico, and many others.</p></noscript>
</main>
<script>
'use strict';
const events=[
{year:1206,date:'1206',name:'A community before an Order',short:'A first home',place:'Prouille, southern France',thread:'Community',object:'The doorway',note:'A place to belong before a movement had a name.',story:'Dominic helped establish a community of women at Prouille. Its life of prayer began before the friars received papal confirmation. The Dominican story does not start with a famous book or a great university. It starts with people making a home for a shared vocation.',prompt:'If you were beginning something good, what would you build first: a home, a school, or a meeting place? Why?',x:12},
{year:1216,date:'1216',name:'A mission gets its name',short:'Order of Preachers',place:'Rome · confirmation by Honorius III',thread:'Preaching',object:'The sealed letter',note:'Official recognition, not an instant worldwide network.',story:'Pope Honorius III confirmed Dominic’s community in December 1216. The Order of Preachers brought a distinctive combination into view: communal prayer, serious study, and preaching. The friars would travel, learn, and speak, rather than simply remain in one place.',prompt:'You can carry only one thing to help explain a big idea: a book, a picture, or a story. Which would you choose?',x:23},
{year:1265,date:'c. 1265',name:'Room for a difficult question',short:'Aquinas begins',place:'Italy · Thomas Aquinas',thread:'Study',object:'The open book',note:'A vast work that was left unfinished.',story:'Around 1265, the Dominican Thomas Aquinas began the Summa theologiae. Its articles give objections a serious hearing before developing an answer. Asking a difficult question was not treated as the opposite of faith: careful thought could be part of its service.',prompt:'Name an idea you believe. Can you state a thoughtful objection to it so fairly that someone who disagrees would recognise it?',x:36},
{year:1376,date:'1376',name:'A voice outside the usual rooms',short:'Catherine speaks',place:'Avignon · Catherine of Siena',thread:'Preaching',object:'The carried letter',note:'Influence did not require holding high office.',story:'Catherine of Siena, a Dominican laywoman, travelled to Avignon in 1376 and urged Pope Gregory XI to return to Rome. He returned in 1377. Her letters and advocacy are one part of a complex political and religious story, not a single-handed explanation for the move.',prompt:'What makes someone worth listening to: their title, their courage, their kindness, or the reasons they give?',x:47},
{year:1440,date:'c. 1440',name:'A wall becomes a window',short:'Angelico paints',place:'San Marco, Florence · Fra Angelico',thread:'Art',object:'The painter’s brush',note:'Beauty in a place of ordinary daily prayer.',story:'In the late 1430s and early 1440s, Dominican friar Fra Angelico and his workshop painted frescoes at San Marco. Many were made for the friars’ own spaces, including their cells. Art here was not just a grand public spectacle; it could quietly accompany a person’s prayer.',prompt:'Choose an ordinary wall at home. What image would help you remember something important each time you passed it?',x:59},
{year:1511,date:'1511',name:'The sermon that disturbed the room',short:'Montesinos protests',place:'Hispaniola · Antonio de Montesinos',thread:'Justice',object:'The pulpit',note:'A voice raised against colonial cruelty.',story:'In Advent 1511, Antonio de Montesinos preached against the oppression of Indigenous people by Spanish colonists. He spoke with the support of his Dominican community. This courageous protest belongs inside a history that also includes grave Christian failures and complicity, not outside it.',prompt:'When a whole room accepts something unfair, what might help one person speak up? How could others stand with them?',x:74},
{year:1840,date:'1840',name:'A thread picked up again',short:'Lacordaire returns',place:'France · Henri-Dominique Lacordaire',thread:'Community',object:'The travelling cloak',note:'A new beginning after revolutionary suppression.',story:'After entering the Order and making profession in 1840, Lacordaire returned to France in his Dominican habit and worked to re-establish Dominican life there. A tradition can continue not only by preserving what exists, but by patiently rebuilding what has been lost.',prompt:'Think of a good family tradition. If it disappeared for a generation, what would you need to bring it back?',x:87},
{year:2016,date:'2016',name:'Eight hundred is not the end',short:'The jubilee',place:'Worldwide · the Dominican family',thread:'Community',object:'The lantern',note:'An anniversary can be a starting question.',story:'The Dominican family marked 800 years since the Order’s 1216 confirmation. Friars, nuns, sisters, and lay Dominicans share in its wider life. An anniversary is a chance to look back, but also to ask how prayer, study, and service might take shape in a changed world.',prompt:'If a Dominican from 1216 visited today, what would surprise them most? What human question might still sound familiar?',x:93}
];
const $=s=>document.querySelector(s);let current=0;const seen=new Set();let active='All';
function show(i){current=Number(i);const e=events[current];seen.add(current);$('#time').value=current;$('#time').setAttribute('aria-valuetext',e.date+', '+e.name);
for(const k of ['year','place','object','story','prompt','thread'])$('#'+k).textContent=k==='year'?e.date:e[k];
$('#title').textContent=e.name;$('#objectnote').textContent=e.note;$('#counter').textContent='Window '+(current+1)+' of 8 · move the lantern';$('#artlabel').textContent=e.date+' · '+e.short;$('#marker').style.left=e.x+'%';$('#prev').disabled=current===0;$('#next').disabled=current===7;$('#visited').textContent=seen.size+' / 8 windows explored';
document.querySelectorAll('.stations button').forEach((b,j)=>b.setAttribute('aria-current',String(j===current)));}
events.forEach((e,i)=>{const b=document.createElement('button');const small=document.createElement('small');small.textContent=e.date;b.append(small,document.createTextNode(e.short));b.addEventListener('click',()=>show(i));$('.stations').append(b);for(const id of ['from','to']){const o=document.createElement('option');o.value=i;o.textContent=e.date+' · '+e.short;$('#'+id).append(o);}});
['All','Community','Preaching','Study','Art','Justice'].forEach(t=>{const b=document.createElement('button');b.textContent=t;b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(t==='All'));b.addEventListener('click',()=>{active=t;document.querySelectorAll('.threads button').forEach(x=>x.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(x===b)));document.querySelectorAll('.stations button').forEach((x,i)=>x.classList.toggle('dim',t!=='All'&&events[i].thread!==t));const matches=events.map((e,i)=>e.thread===t?i:-1).filter(i=>i>=0);$('#filterstatus').textContent=t==='All'?'All eight windows are lit. The slider steps between milestones, not equal lengths of time.':matches.length+' '+t.toLowerCase()+' window'+(matches.length===1?'':'s')+' highlighted. All windows remain available.';if(t!=='All'&&events[current].thread!==t)show(matches[0]);});$('.threads').append(b);});
$('#time').addEventListener('input',e=>show(e.target.value));$('#prev').onclick=()=>show(Math.max(0,current-1));$('#next').onclick=()=>show(Math.min(7,current+1));
$('#from').value='1';$('#to').value='7';
function compare(){const a=events[Number($('#from').value)],b=events[Number($('#to').value)],gap=Math.abs(a.year-b.year);$('#gap').replaceChildren(document.createTextNode(gap));const small=document.createElement('small');small.textContent='YEARS APART';$('#gap').append(small);const approximate=a.date.startsWith('c.')||b.date.startsWith('c.');$('#comparison').textContent=gap===0?'The same window: no time between these two views.':(approximate?'About ':'')+gap+' years: '+(gap/25).toFixed(1)+' imagined 25-year generations. '+(gap<30?'A change within one lifetime.':'Enough time for people to inherit a tradition they never saw begin.');$('#interval').style.left=((Math.min(a.year,b.year)-1206)/810*100)+'%';$('#interval').style.width=(gap/810*100)+'%';}
$('#from').onchange=compare;$('#to').onchange=compare;
$('#restart').onclick=()=>{seen.clear();document.querySelector('.threads button').click();$('#from').value='1';$('#to').value='7';compare();show(0);};
$('#print').onclick=()=>{const paper=$('#paper');paper.replaceChildren();const h=document.createElement('h1');h.textContent='My Dominican lantern journey';paper.append(h);events.forEach((e,i)=>{if(!seen.has(i))return;const title=document.createElement('h2');title.textContent=e.date+' · '+e.name;const p=document.createElement('p');p.textContent=e.story;paper.append(title,p);});const end=document.createElement('p');end.textContent='Inspired by Jon’s Timeline of Dominican History. A selective companion made by Chloe. Dates marked c. are approximate.';paper.append(end);window.print();};
show(0);compare();
</script></body></html>
